Chat.responseParamsDescription:
#### Ext fields

**When `AnswerSource` is `BotFramework`:**

| Parameter             | Type    | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| --------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| MATCHED_ENTRY_NAME    | String  | The name of the matched trigger node.                                                                                                                                                                       |
| MATCHED_INTENT_SOURCE | String  | The intent source of the matched trigger node.                                                                                                                                                              |
| INTENT_ID             | Long    | The ID of the matched intent.                                                                                                                                                                               |
| IntentName            | String  | Same as `INTENT_NAME`.                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| INTENT_DETAIL         | String  | Describes how the intent was matched. This field is useful when INTENT_SOURCE is Similarity or Lgf. For Similarity, it contains the matched intent utterance. For Lgf, it contains the matched LGF grammar. |
| IS_SESSION_FINISHED   | Boolean | Indicates whether the session has finished.                                                                                                                                                                 |
| DsScore               | String  | The confidence score for the matched dialog flow. Also returned as dsScore.                                                                                                                                 |
| DIALOG_ID             | String  | The ID of the dialog flow.                                                                                                                                                                                  |
| FINISH_LABEL          | Boolean | Indicates if the response node is a final node. This is a business-defined value, typically used for analytics.                                                                                             |
| MODULE_START          | Boolean | Indicates whether this is the starting intent node of a dialog flow.                                                                                                                                        |
| INTENT_NAME           | String  | The name of the matched intent.                                                                                                                                                                             |
| INTENT_SOURCE         | String  | The method used for intent recognition. Valid values include: `Similarity` for similarity matching, `Lgf` for LGF grammar matching, and `Classify` for supervised model matching.                           |
| DIALOG_NAME           | String  | The name of the dialog flow.                                                                                                                                                                                |
| DS_REPORT             | Map     | Contains key-value pairs for variables selected for "Output to report" in the dialog flow configuration.                                                                                                    |
| TASK_ID               | String  | The task ID returned by the asynchronous service.                                                                                                                                                           |

